<section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow" data-i18n="ld.eyebrow">Live demo · A real, read-only sandbox of the app <span class="pill pill-built" data-i18n="ld.pill">No login</span></p>
      <h1 data-i18n="ld.h1">Try openWCS right here, <span class="lime">no sign-up, nothing saved.</span></h1>
      <p class="lead" data-i18n="ld.lead">
        This is the real openWCS app running entirely in your browser as a read-only sandbox. Open every
        menu and browse the actual screens with sample data, but nothing can be changed and nothing is
        saved anywhere. Reloading the page resets the demo to its starting point. The headline interaction
        is the goods-to-person pick station: five totes arrive and you can pick them, full pick or short
        pick, including the normal exceptions.
      </p>
      <div class="grid grid-3">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head"><div class="tag" data-i18n="ld.point1Tag">Read-only</div></div>
          <h3 data-i18n="ld.point1H">Browse everything, change nothing</h3>
          <p data-i18n="ld.point1P">Every menu opens and every screen renders with sample data, but all create, edit and delete controls are disabled. You cannot break anything.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head"><div class="tag" data-i18n="ld.point2Tag">Nothing saved</div></div>
          <h3 data-i18n="ld.point2H">It all lives in your browser</h3>
          <p data-i18n="ld.point2P">There is no backend and no database behind this demo. All state is in memory, so a page reload restores the original sample data and re-arms the five totes.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head"><div class="tag" data-i18n="ld.point3Tag">Pick five totes</div></div>
          <h3 data-i18n="ld.point3H">The goods-to-person station</h3>
          <p data-i18n="ld.point3P">Five totes arrive at the pick station. Present and confirm each one as a full pick or a short pick, trigger the usual exceptions, and reset to run it again. The demo carries a station of each pick layout: one-to-one, one-to-N lit slots, and a put-wall, with the slot and light states rendered.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ld-guide-section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow" data-i18n="ld.guideEyebrow">A two-minute tour</p>
      <h2 data-i18n="ld.guideH">Not sure where to start? Do this.</h2>
      <p class="lead" data-i18n="ld.guideLead">The sandbox is a read-only snapshot, so most screens are there to browse. The one thing you can actually drive is the pick station, so start there, then dip into the menus that carry sample data.</p>

      <div class="grid grid-2">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head"><div class="tag" data-i18n="ld.guideStationTag">The main event</div></div>
          <h3 data-i18n="ld.guideStationH">Pick five totes at PP1</h3>
          <ol class="steps">
            <li data-i18n="ld.guideStep1">Open <strong>Operations, then GTP workplaces</strong> in the left menu and choose <strong>PP1 (Pick Place 1)</strong>.</li>
            <li data-i18n="ld.guideStep2">Claim the station. Five totes are already inducted and roll into the queue in front of you.</li>
            <li data-i18n="ld.guideStep3">For each tote, present the stock, then confirm a <strong>full pick</strong>, or enter a lower number for a <strong>short pick</strong>.</li>
            <li data-i18n="ld.guideStep4">Try an exception: mark a tote dirty, or report some units broken, and watch the cycle adapt.</li>
            <li data-i18n="ld.guideStep5">Clear all five, then hit <strong>Restart demo</strong> in the top banner to run it again.</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="ld-guide-note" data-i18n="ld.guideLayouts">Want the other layouts? <strong>PP2</strong> is a one-to-N station with lit slots and <strong>PW1</strong> is a put-wall with pick-to-light, each rendering its own slot and light states.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head"><div class="tag" data-i18n="ld.guideDataTag">Worth a look</div></div>
          <h3 data-i18n="ld.guideDataH">Menus that carry sample data</h3>
          <ul class="ld-guide-list">
            <li data-i18n="ld.guideData1"><strong>Overview</strong>, the landing page: live tiles for stock, inbound, outbound, dispatch and automation.</li>
            <li data-i18n="ld.guideData2"><strong>Dashboards:</strong> Stock levels, ABC movers, Replenishment and the full-screen Andon board.</li>
            <li data-i18n="ld.guideData3"><strong>Operations:</strong> Stock overview, Handling units, Stock counting, Picking and Transport.</li>
            <li data-i18n="ld.guideData4"><strong>Reporting:</strong> Material flow, ASRS, Stock, Inbound and Outbound charts.</li>
            <li data-i18n="ld.guideData5"><strong>Master data:</strong> Warehouses, SKUs, Locations, Areas, Storage blocks and HU types.</li>
            <li data-i18n="ld.guideData6"><strong>Engineering:</strong> Slotting, the Process designer and the 3D Automation topology.</li>
            <li data-i18n="ld.guideData7"><strong>Administration:</strong> the Database browser, Users and Warehouse access.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="ld-guide-note" data-i18n="ld.guideEmptyNote">Screens we did not snapshot show a clean empty state rather than an error, so open anything you like.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

